DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:amavasya-2026-11-09@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:purnima-amavasya\,ancestral
DESCRIPTION:Why: when the moon is dark\, turn attention to those who came b
 efore.\n\nStory: Amavasya is the new-moon tithi — traditionally linked w
 ith ancestral remembrance (pitru) and quieter household rites.\nSource: Ga
 ruda Purana ancestral strands\; panchanga practice\nWhy: when the moon is 
 dark\, turn attention to those who came before.\nModern angle: Scheduled g
 rief/remembrance days aid mourning culture\; cultural/psychological.\nEvid
 ence: Cultural/psychological\nMore: https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharma
 setu/review/reasoning.html#shraddha-remembrance\nLocation basis: New Delhi
 . City-specific timing coming later.
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
